Sure! Below is a simple example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML & CSS.  
When you hover over the card, it rotates 180° around its Y‑axis.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* The card itself – front + back */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;/* Smooth rotation */
}

/* Hover triggers rotation */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front side */
.front,
.back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside when facing away */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #fff;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
}

.front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b); /* Warm gradient */
}

.back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43cea2, #185a9d); /* Cool gradient */
    transform: rotateY(180deg); /* Flip so it's visible after rotation */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front face -->
        <div class="front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
        </div>
        <!-- Back face -->
        <div class="back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets the `perspective`, giving the illusion of depth. |
| `.card` | Holds both sides; `transform-style: preserve-3d` allows child elements to maintain their 3D positions. |
| `.front` / `.back` | Each side is absolutely positioned on top of each other. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that's turned away from the viewer. |
| Hover rule (`.card:hover`) | Rotates the whole card 180° around the Y‑axis. |

Feel free to replace the gradients or add images/text inside the `<h2>` tags to customize the card’s appearance. Enjoy experimenting with different angles, durations, or easing functions!
